---
layout: layouts/base.njk
title: Software
description: Explore the software we build, from released RepoPact and SkillForge packages to early planning tools and private ForgeWire and Fabric development.
permalink: /projects/index.html
---
<section class="page-lead page-shell" aria-labelledby="projects-title">
  <p class="eyebrow">ForgeWire Labs · Software</p>
  <h1 id="projects-title">Built for <em>different jobs.</em></h1>
  <p class="lead-copy">We build repository tools, intelligent workspaces, distributed execution infrastructure, communication software, planning tools, and technical learning applications. They aren't all parts of one required stack. Here you'll find what's released, what's in preview, and what we're still developing privately.</p>
  <p class="lead-index"><span>Released software</span><span>Previews</span><span>Private development</span></p>
</section>

<section class="repository-spread page-shell" aria-labelledby="repopact-title">
  <div class="spread-heading">
    <p class="eyebrow">ForgeWire Labs · Repository systems</p>
    <h2 id="repopact-title">RepoPact</h2>
    <p>RepoPact keeps the decisions behind the code available to the next contributor. Core owns repository governance and validation; Workbench provides a separate native interface using the same rules.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="repo-product-grid">
    {% for project in projects %}{% if project.id == "repopact-core" or project.id == "repopact-workbench" %}
      <article class="product-entry product-entry--{{ project.statusKind }}" data-project-id="{{ project.id }}">
        <div class="product-entry-top"><span>{{ project.kicker }}</span><span class="status status--{{ project.statusKind }}">{{ project.status }}</span></div>
        <h3><a href="{{ project.url }}">{{ project.name }} <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></h3>
        <p>{{ project.summary }}</p>
        <p class="availability-copy"><strong>Current status.</strong> {{ project.maturity }}</p>
        <div class="product-entry-links"><a href="{{ project.url }}">{{ project.action }} <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>{% if project.secondaryUrl %}<a href="{{ project.secondaryUrl }}">{{ project.secondaryAction }} <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>{% endif %}</div>
      </article>
    {% endif %}{% endfor %}
  </div>
  <div class="repo-evidence-grid">
    <figure class="architecture-figure architecture-figure--page">
      <img src="{{ site.basePath }}/assets/repopact-architecture.svg" alt="RepoPact Core architecture: repository records connect to a canonical Rust engine, which serves CLI and Workbench clients and produces evidence and derived views. An optional host or CI integration has a provider-specific boundary." aria-describedby="repopact-diagram-notes" width="1200" height="720" loading="lazy">
      <figcaption>How RepoPact works: source records remain authoritative, Core interprets them, and clients provide different ways to work with them. See the <a href="https://github.com/ForgeWireLabs/repopact-core/blob/614689b127cf52f801877cc48440f7e45c3709eb/docs/assets/readme/repopact-architecture.svg">public architecture documentation</a>.</figcaption>
      <p class="diagram-notes" id="repopact-diagram-notes"><strong>Diagram key.</strong> Blue arrows show exchanges with the Core engine; slate arrows show people, host integrations, evidence, and derived views; dashed boxes mark derived views. The host/CI box is optional and provider-specific. <a href="{{ site.basePath }}/assets/repopact-architecture.svg">Open the full-size diagram</a>.</p>
    </figure>
    <figure class="screenshot-figure">
      <div class="screenshot-focus screenshot-frame--light"><img src="{{ site.basePath }}/assets/workbench-desktop-dashboard.jpg" alt="RepoPact Workbench desktop capture focused on its repository validation summary. The capture was made from a Windows x64 source build." width="1362" height="930" loading="lazy"></div>
      <figcaption><strong>RepoPact Workbench · Source-build preview.</strong> Windows x64 source build with disposable Core conformance records. The visible counts are test data, not customer or production metrics. Packaged installers are not listed. <a href="{{ site.basePath }}/assets/workbench-desktop-dashboard.jpg">Open the full-resolution capture</a> · <a href="https://github.com/ForgeWireLabs/repopact-workbench/blob/414a4a78091796735a1b97b03fd8c3cf1c105f30/docs/assets/readme/workbench-desktop-dashboard.jpg">View its source and provenance ↗</a></figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="private-section" aria-labelledby="private-title">
  <div class="page-shell">
    <div class="private-heading">
      <p class="eyebrow">Research and private development</p>
      <h2 id="private-title">What we're developing privately.</h2>
      <p>ForgeWire and Fabric have public technical overviews, but we aren't offering public application builds or supported deployments yet.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="private-register">
      {% for project in projects %}{% if project.group == "private" %}
        <article class="private-record" data-project-id="{{ project.id }}">
          <p class="eyebrow">{{ project.kicker }}</p>
          <h3>{% if project.url %}<a href="{{ project.url }}">{{ project.name }} <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>{% else %}{{ project.name }}{% endif %}</h3>
          <p>{{ project.summary }}</p>
          <p class="availability-copy"><strong>{{ project.status }}.</strong> {{ project.maturity }}</p>
          {% if project.url %}<a class="text-link" href="{{ project.url }}">{{ project.action }} <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>{% endif %}
        </article>
      {% endif %}{% endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="planning-spread page-shell" aria-labelledby="anvil-title">
  <div class="planning-copy">
    <p class="eyebrow">ForgeWire Labs · Planning</p>
  </div>
  {% for project in projects %}{% if project.id == "anvil" %}
    <article class="planning-entry" data-project-id="{{ project.id }}">
      <div class="product-entry-top"><span>{{ project.kicker }}</span><span class="status status--{{ project.statusKind }}">{{ project.status }}</span></div>
      <h2 id="anvil-title"><a href="{{ project.url }}">{{ project.name }} <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></h2>
      <p class="planning-summary">{{ project.summary }}</p>
      <p class="availability-copy"><strong>Current status.</strong> {{ project.maturity }}</p>
      <a class="text-link" href="{{ project.url }}">{{ project.action }} <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
    </article>
  {% endif %}{% endfor %}
</section>

<section class="communication-section" aria-labelledby="flink-title">
  <div class="page-shell communication-layout">
    <div class="communication-copy">
      <p class="eyebrow">ForgeWire Labs · Communications</p>
      {% for project in projects %}{% if project.id == "flink" %}
        <div data-project-id="{{ project.id }}">
          <div class="product-entry-top"><span>{{ project.kicker }}</span><span class="status status--{{ project.statusKind }}">{{ project.status }}</span></div>
          <h2 id="flink-title"><a href="{{ project.url }}">{{ project.name }} <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></h2>
          <p>{{ project.summary }}</p>
          <p class="availability-copy"><strong>Current status.</strong> {{ project.maturity }}</p>
          <div class="product-entry-links"><a href="{{ project.url }}">{{ project.action }} <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a href="{{ project.secondaryUrl }}">{{ project.secondaryAction }} <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
        </div>
      {% endif %}{% endfor %}
    </div>
    <figure class="flink-figure">
      <img src="{{ site.basePath }}/assets/flink-product-architecture.svg" alt="Flink's documented product model shows a human operator, communication cockpit, governed API and MCP boundary, providers as channel edges, and ForgeWire or Fabric as optional integration edges." aria-describedby="flink-diagram-notes" width="1500" height="1000" loading="lazy">
      <figcaption>Flink owns communication and human decision state. Providers connect as channels; agents and applications enter through governed interfaces. This public product-model diagram predates the Flink rename, and the current packaged release still uses ForgeLink naming. Dashed lines show optional integrations, not verified implementations. <a href="{{ site.basePath }}/assets/flink-product-architecture.svg">Open the full-size diagram</a>.</figcaption>
      <p class="diagram-notes" id="flink-diagram-notes">The diagram labels solid lines as Flink ownership and dashed lines as optional edges. It describes Flink only; it does not imply a shared architecture across ForgeWire Labs projects.</p>
    </figure>
  </div>
</section>

